cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite version 0.3.0-preprint for the preliminary, unrefereed upper-bound
  manuscript. It is not independently verified by human reviewers. Zenodo
  assigns an immutable version DOI after GitHub ingestion; the concept DOI
  identifies the lineage.
title: "An upper density bound for sets avoiding reciprocal triples"
type: software
version: "0.3.0-preprint"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Khanukov
    given-names: Dmitry
repository-code: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302/releases/tag/v0.3.0-corrected-preprint"
url: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
abstract: >-
  The computer-assisted proof bounds the upper limiting density of subsets
  avoiding three distinct integers a, b, c with 1/a = 1/b + 1/c strictly
  below 0.830783022367. Cold and exterior replay at proof-source commit
  4abf9b466b3e0d920ce918a8a7d7579ed4cf34ae passed in GitHub Actions run 44830958575.
  The cold run regenerated 3,094,631 positive correction cells and matched
  the recorded SHA-256 digest. C++17 and Python verify the finite witnesses;
  Lean checks the counting argument and exact arithmetic, with explicit
  finite-witness hypotheses at the endpoint. This does not determine the
  density or solve Erdős Problem 302. The work is preliminary, unrefereed,
  and not independently verified or peer reviewed. AI systems assisted with
  search, code, formalization, and audits; the author is responsible for all
  claims. Original software and verification material are MIT-licensed and
  original manuscript material is CC BY 4.0 under LICENSE_SCOPE.md. Zenodo
  archives tagged source; the checked release assets remain on GitHub.
